        "For admission in India, an IB Diploma or a Cambridge or Edexcel qualification is generally accepted on the basis of an equivalence certificate from the Association of Indian Universities. The AIU treats the IGCSE as comparable to Class 10 and the IB Diploma as comparable to Class 12. Ask each university when it wants the certificate, since some want it at application and others at admission, and begin the paperwork before results day.",
        "CUET-UG is the main gateway to central universities and many others, and students with IB or IGCSE-based qualifications can apply where the subjects line up with a university's requirements. Check the current CUET bulletin and each course's eligibility page every year, because subject combinations and rules change. The IB subject mix chosen in Class 11 should be checked against the courses in mind at the start, when it can still be changed.",
