        "Core and Extended are about the ceiling, not just the difficulty: Cambridge Core papers cap the grade below the top, while Extended papers open the full scale. Edexcel uses Foundation and Higher tiers in a similar way. For a student who might go on to IB Mathematics or a science at Higher Level, Extended or Higher is normally the sensible target, and deciding early avoids a painful tier change a few months before the exam.",
