  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find IB and IGCSE tutors in Thakurdwara?", answer: "Send IB Gram the board, programme, subject, level and exam series, and a shortlist of tutors who have taught that exact course comes back. This is how IB and IGCSE tutors in Thakurdwara are matched: on syllabus fit, not postcode, because every lesson runs online. The first lesson is free, and a different tutor is arranged if the first pairing does not suit your child." },
    { question: "Do IB and IGCSE tutors visit homes in Thakurdwara?", answer: "No. Tutors do not visit homes in Thakurdwara, because in-person visits are offered only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. Here, private lessons are live and online, one to one, taken from your own home on a laptop or tablet. A shared whiteboard and scanned past papers replace the table and notebook, and the tutor can be anywhere in India." },
    { question: "Is there an IB or IGCSE school in Thakurdwara or Kashipur?", answer: "We could not confirm one in either place. Thakurdwara's schools largely follow the UP Board and CBSE, while Kashipur's follow the Uttarakhand Board, CBSE and ICSE. The nearest confirmed options are boarding and day schools in Dehradun, Mussoorie and Delhi NCR. Please verify any school's current programmes and admissions with the school itself before planning around it." },
    { question: "Can my child study IGCSE privately while attending a UP Board or CBSE school?", answer: "Yes, for Cambridge and Edexcel IGCSE, provided an approved exam centre accepts the candidate. The child studies the syllabus with an online tutor and sits the papers at the centre. Private candidates usually take a written alternative to the science practical, and entry deadlines fall months before each series, so settle the board, subjects and centre early." },
    { question: "Can the IB Diploma be studied privately from Thakurdwara?", answer: "No. The Diploma can only be taken by a student registered through an authorised IB World School, so no private candidate route exists. A family set on it is looking at a school elsewhere, often as a boarder, for example at Woodstock School in Mussoorie or at a school in Delhi NCR. Tutoring can prepare a student beforehand and support them alongside the school's teaching." },
    { question: "What does IB or IGCSE tuition cost for a Thakurdwara family?", answer: "The rate depends on programme and level, subject, session length, the tutor's recent experience with that syllabus and how near the exam is. It is confirmed in writing before the trial lesson, so there are no surprises. Distance does not add to it, since nothing is in person. Higher Level Diploma subjects and scarce IGCSE subjects generally cost more than MYP or Core work." },
    { question: "Does the first lesson really cost nothing?", answer: "Yes. The free trial is a real lesson on a topic from your child's own syllabus, taught live by the tutor proposed for the job. Afterwards you receive a short plan for the first month. You can continue, ask for changes or request another tutor, with no obligation attached to the trial itself." },
    { question: "Which IGCSE board should a Thakurdwara student choose, Cambridge or Edexcel?", answer: "Choose whichever board the student's exam centre or school offers for the subjects needed, then stay with it. Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel cover similar content but differ in paper style, timing and tier structure. If both are available, the student's strengths and the series dates usually decide it, and a tutor can show sample papers from each." },
    { question: "Will a tutor help with my child's Internal Assessment or Extended Essay?", answer: "Tutors coach; they never write. They help a student choose a workable question, understand the criteria, plan the method and review drafts honestly, but they do not write, rewrite or complete any Internal Assessment, Extended Essay, TOK essay or coursework, because that would breach the rules of the IB and the IGCSE boards." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you teach a Thakurdwara student?", answer: "Both Mathematics courses, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Environmental Systems and Societies, Economics, Business Management, Computer Science, Psychology, Geography, English A, Hindi and Theory of Knowledge are covered, at Higher or Standard Level. If your subject is unusual, send the exact course name and level and we will say honestly whether a suitable tutor is available." },
    { question: "Do you tutor MYP and PYP students as well as Diploma students?", answer: "Yes, the whole IB continuum is covered. PYP sessions build reading, number sense and the habit of asking investigable questions. MYP sessions focus on criterion-based writing, science skills and the Personal Project process. Younger children usually do better with shorter sessions, and parents receive a written note after each one." },
    { question: "How do fog or a power cut affect online lessons in Thakurdwara?", answer: "Fog mostly disrupts travel, not lessons, which is one advantage of learning online; a dropped connection or power cut is the real risk. Keep a phone hotspot and a charged laptop ready, tell the tutor as early as possible if a lesson is lost, and agree a replacement slot. Fog-season sessions sit better in afternoons and evenings than at dawn." },
    { question: "When should a Thakurdwara student start IB or IGCSE tuition?", answer: "Starting when the course begins works well: Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma. A student planning a boarding move can start in Class 9 or 10 to build mathematical depth and academic English ahead of time. A later start still helps if the work targets the highest-value topics and timed papers rather than trying to cover everything." },
    { question: "My child will join an IB or IGCSE school in Delhi NCR or Dehradun. Can tutoring start before the move?", answer: "Yes, and it is often the smartest time to begin. A tutor can close gaps against the new school's syllabus, introduce its marking style and build English writing stamina before the first term. After the move, sessions continue online alongside the school's own teaching, with notes shared so that nothing is repeated." },
    { question: "Can my child study Hindi or Urdu for IB or IGCSE credit?", answer: "Often yes. The IB offers Hindi as both a Language A literature and a Language B course, and Cambridge offers Hindi and Urdu as second languages at IGCSE. Whether a school or centre can enter a student for a given language depends on its own arrangements, so confirm that first. Tutors can then prepare the speaking, reading and writing tasks." },
    { question: "What if my child and the tutor are not a good fit?", answer: "Say so, and another tutor is arranged. A trial that falls flat costs nothing, and a change later in the term is also possible. Regular check-ins every few weeks are meant to catch a poor fit early, so a child is not left struggling with someone who does not suit them." },
  ],

